From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Douglas Panhota <douglaspands@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: keep an OTG port without VBUS sensing powered

On the R36S V5 (RK3326) the PHY never sees VBUS of the OTG connector:
utmi_bvalid stays low with a PC on the cable. The OTG state machine
powers the port off on its first run (OTG_STATE_UNDEFINED without VBUS)
and only powers it on again for a host (ID low) or a detected VBUS. The
dwc2 controller, put in peripheral mode by its USB role switch, then has
no PHY clock: binding a gadget logs

  dwc2 ff300000.usb: dwc2_core_reset: HANG! Soft Reset timeout GRSTCTL_CSFTRST
  dwc2 ff300000.usb: dwc2_wait_for_mode: Couldn't set device mode

and the PC never sees the device.

With "rockchip,vbus-always-on" on the otg-port node, the state machine
does not power the port off for lack of VBUS, neither on its first run
nor when a host cable is removed. The ID pin handling (extcon USB-HOST)
is unchanged, so the role can still follow the ID pin.

The B-session valid signal is ignored too. On the R36S V5 it does rise
with a charger on the separate DC connector, and the state machine then
ran charger detection on the data lines of the OTG port (where a PC is)
and dropped the gadget: plugging the charger disconnected the console
from the PC for good. The RK817 detects the charger on its own.

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
index 8f4c08e..a4ca3ad 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@ struct rockchip_usb2phy_port {
 	unsigned int	port_id;
 	bool		suspended;
 	bool		vbus_attached;
+	bool		vbus_always_on;
 	bool            host_disconnect;
 	int		bvalid_irq;
 	int		id_irq;
@@ -666,7 +667,14 @@ static void rockchip_usb2phy_otg_sm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	unsigned long delay;
 	bool vbus_attach, sch_work, notify_charger;

-	vbus_attach = property_enabled(rphy->grf,
+	/*
+	 * A port without VBUS sensing of its own may still see a B-session from
+	 * another connector (the DC charger input of the R36S V5); charger
+	 * detection would then run on the data lines of this port and power it
+	 * off. Ignore the signal: the controller decides the role.
+	 */
+	vbus_attach = !rport->vbus_always_on &&
+		      property_enabled(rphy->grf,
 				       &rport->port_cfg->utmi_bvalid);

 	sch_work = false;
@@ -678,7 +686,7 @@ static void rockchip_usb2phy_otg_sm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	switch (rport->state) {
 	case OTG_STATE_UNDEFINED:
 		rport->state = OTG_STATE_B_IDLE;
-		if (!vbus_attach)
+		if (!vbus_attach && !rport->vbus_always_on)
 			rockchip_usb2phy_power_off(rport->phy);
 		fallthrough;
 	case OTG_STATE_B_IDLE:
@@ -759,7 +767,8 @@ static void rockchip_usb2phy_otg_sm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		if (extcon_get_state(rphy->edev, EXTCON_USB_HOST) == 0) {
 			dev_dbg(&rport->phy->dev, "usb otg host disconnect\n");
 			rport->state = OTG_STATE_B_IDLE;
-			rockchip_usb2phy_power_off(rport->phy);
+			if (!rport->vbus_always_on)
+				rockchip_usb2phy_power_off(rport->phy);
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -1298,6 +1307,10 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_otg_port_init(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy,
 	 */
 	rport->suspended = true;
 	rport->vbus_attached = false;
+	rport->vbus_always_on = of_property_read_bool(child_np,
+						      "rockchip,vbus-always-on");
+	if (rport->vbus_always_on)
+		dev_info(rphy->dev, "otg port: no VBUS sensing, kept powered\n");

 	mutex_init(&rport->mutex);

